---
// "Before you read on": the paragraph that earns the rest of the page.
---
<section id="before" class="lp-section">
  <div class="lp-shell">
    <div class="before-body">
      <div class="before-rail">
        <p class="lp-eyebrow">Before you read on</p>
      </div>

      <div class="before-main" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="lp-h2 before-head">
          Most letters like this are not worth your time. This one might be.
        </h2>
        <p>
          You probably get letters like this. Someone wants the garden that has become another
          job, the garage nobody uses, or the strip beside the house, and the figure they quote is
          rarely based on anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          I write differently. I write to five landowners a week, and I have looked at each site
          before writing. I explain in plain terms what it could be worth with planning permission
          and what I am offering.
        </p>
        <p>
          You do not owe me a reply. Doing nothing is a perfectly good answer, and I will not chase
          you for one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .before-body {
    padding: 64px 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .before-main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .before-main p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .before-head {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--lp-ink-display);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .before-body {
      padding: 128px 0;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
      column-gap: 32px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
